message: "If you use this software or experimental paradigm in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Unity linear-maze EEG paradigm"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Cervera Ferri"
    given-names: "Ana"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2300-5571"
    affiliation: "Universitat de València"

  - family-names: "Lloret"
    given-names: "Ana"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0266-0304"
    affiliation: "Universitat de València"

repository-code: "https://github.com/anacervera/eeg-linear-maze-unity"

abstract: >
  Unity-based visuospatial audiovisual experimental paradigm developed
  for EEG research. The paradigm combines repeated first-person traversal
  through three spatial contexts with audiovisual instrument associations
  and a subsequent visual recognition test. During the third traversal,
  the instrument associated with the second spatial context changes,
  introducing a violation of the previously established context-stimulus
  association.

keywords:
  - EEG
  - cognitive neuroscience
  - visuospatial processing
  - audiovisual association
  - experimental paradigm
  - Unity
  - recognition memory
